From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARMJIT: hot ranges keep an index of their blocks' masks

A write into a range with a hot self-modifying granule (patch 0017) scanned every block of the 512 bytes
(~67 in Golden Sun: Dark Dawn's ITCM, each a cache miss) to find the few that hold the written 16 bytes.
Such ranges now keep their blocks with their masks side by side, kept exactly in step with the range's
block list; the per-block teardown is InvalidateBlock, shared by both paths. Frames and audio identical
with MELONDS_JIT_HOTIDX=0 (the old scan).
---
--- a/src/ARMJIT.h
+++ b/src/ARMJIT.h
@@ -110,6 +110,11 @@
     std::unordered_map<u32, u32> SmcDrops {};
     std::vector<u32> HotSmc {};
     bool IsHotSmc(u32 localAddr) const noexcept;
+    // (patch 0018) the hot granules' 512-byte ranges: each one's blocks with their masks there, side by side, so a
+    // write scans these instead of every block's own memory (the blocks of a range are kept here exactly as in it)
+    std::unordered_map<AddressRange*, std::vector<std::pair<JitBlock*, u32>>> HotRangeIdx {};
+    void InvalidateBlock(JitBlock* block, AddressRange* range, AddressRange* region, u32 localAddr) noexcept;
+    void IndexRange(AddressRange* range, u32 rangeAddr) noexcept;
 
 
     AddressRange CodeIndexITCM[ITCMPhysicalSize / 512] {};
